{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,16.401,1.643,1.471,"Commodities Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"20 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,7.45,3.651,3.268,"Gold"],[13.889,14.731,34.637,2.373,2.124,"An 8% week that rates do not explain"],[13.889,20.845,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Gold settled at $3,685.50 on 19 November, down 7.9% in the week since our"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"last note and 31% below its 29 January record; it last settled this low in"],[13.889,23.733,52.966,1.809,1.634,"September 2025. October’s Fed minutes, out on 18 November, showed nearly all"],[13.889,25.177,52.934,1.809,1.634,"officials expect to raise rates again, and futures price a December hike. Yet rates"],[13.889,26.621,52.951,1.809,1.634,"moved little: the 10-year real yield rose 10bp, to 2.88%, and the dollar 0.9%."],[13.889,28.065,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Our model, fitted to weekly changes over 2006-23, takes 3.8% off gold per"],[13.889,29.509,48.049,1.809,1.634,"100bp on real yields and 1.0% per 1% on the dollar: 1.3 points of the fall."],[13.889,31.995,52.931,1.809,1.634,"The rest is a premium deflating; since the record, rates and the dollar explain 11"],[13.889,33.439,52.954,1.809,1.634,"points of a 31% fall. From end-2023 to the record gold rose 157%, against 24%"],[13.889,34.883,52.936,1.809,1.634,"from rates, the dollar and an 8% a year drift. Of that excess, 44% has gone, yet"],[13.889,36.328,52.931,1.809,1.634,"gold trades 51% above the model path of $2,440, level with the 1980 peak in"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"today’s dollars. The official bid has held: central banks bought 675t in nine"],[13.889,39.216,52.936,1.809,1.634,"months, 6% more than a year earlier, though only 120t of the third quarter’s 321t"],[13.889,40.684,52.966,1.809,1.634,"was reported and the first quarter was revised from 244t to 57t. Jewellery fell"],[13.889,42.128,28.625,1.809,1.634,"17% and bars and coins 19% in the quarter."],[13.889,44.59,52.931,1.809,1.634,"We stay Neutral with a Dec-27 target of $4,150 (was $4,400), 13% above the"],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"price: the weighted value of three unchanged cases. Base (50%): two more Fed"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"hikes, real yields ease to 2.4%, the premium holds: $4,220. Bull (25%): the Fed"],[13.889,48.946,52.966,1.809,1.634,"reverses, real yields return to 1.9%, the premium rebuilds: $4,950. Bear (25%):"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"real yields reach 3.25% and half the premium goes: $3,150. The target fell with"],[13.889,51.834,52.931,1.809,1.634,"the price because the model takes the premium where it stands. Positioning is no"],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"floor: managed money was at the 33rd percentile of its three-year range on 10"],[13.889,54.722,52.992,1.809,1.634,"November. In rupees the fall from the record is 24%, cushioned by May’s duty"],[13.889,56.167,7.884,1.809,1.634,"rise to 15%."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.451,68.023,2.306,1.022,0.915,"3,000"],[14.451,65.409,2.306,1.022,0.915,"4,000"],[14.451,62.807,2.306,1.022,0.915,"5,000"],[14.451,60.195,2.306,1.022,0.915,"6,000"],[17.882,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.506,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.374,68.717,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[31.983,68.717,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[17.504,69.888,4.439,1.275,1.111,"Gold ($/oz)"],[24.724,69.888,9.893,1.275,1.111,"Gold in rupees (rebased)"],[20.481,71.048,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.948,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.864,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.048,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[14.91,72.114,2.063,1.387,1.209,"USD"],[18.98,72.114,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−15.1%"],[23.896,72.114,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−11.4%"],[28.811,72.114,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−18.9%"],[33.497,72.114,2.842,1.387,1.209,"−9.7%"],[15.277,73.179,1.696,1.387,1.209,"INR"],[19.532,73.179,2.842,1.387,1.209,"−4.1%"],[23.896,73.179,3.394,1.3